# HELP mqttd_append_lane_jobs Durable-append lane jobs admitted and not yet completed, summed over sessions (issue #242); sustained growth means a placement group's followers are not keeping up — the warning before publish_dropped{reason="append-backlog-full"} fires.
# TYPE mqttd_append_lane_jobs gauge
mqttd_append_lane_jobs 0
# HELP mqttd_sessions Known client sessions (connected or retained).
# TYPE mqttd_sessions gauge
mqttd_sessions 0
# HELP mqttd_subscriptions Active topic-filter subscriptions across all sessions.
# TYPE mqttd_subscriptions gauge
mqttd_subscriptions 0
# HELP mqttd_retained_messages Retained messages held by the broker.
# TYPE mqttd_retained_messages gauge
mqttd_retained_messages 0
# HELP mqttd_inflight_messages Unacknowledged QoS>0 messages outstanding to clients.
# TYPE mqttd_inflight_messages gauge
mqttd_inflight_messages 0
# HELP mqttd_backlog_bytes Accounted bytes held in flow-control backlogs across sessions (sampled on the session sweep, not live).
# TYPE mqttd_backlog_bytes gauge
mqttd_backlog_bytes 0
# HELP mqttd_backlog_bytes_max Accounted bytes held by the LARGEST single session's flow-control backlog (sampled on the session sweep, not live) — the number to size a PER-SUBSCRIBER cap against, since backlog_bytes sums every session.
# TYPE mqttd_backlog_bytes_max gauge
mqttd_backlog_bytes_max 0
# HELP mqttd_cluster_members Cluster members eligible for placement (this node plus non-dead peers).
# TYPE mqttd_cluster_members gauge
mqttd_cluster_members 3
# HELP mqttd_peer_links Currently connected inter-node peer links.
# TYPE mqttd_peer_links gauge
mqttd_peer_links 2
# HELP mqttd_peer_forwards_in_flight Frames queued on inter-node peer links, not yet written to the wire.
# TYPE mqttd_peer_forwards_in_flight gauge
mqttd_peer_forwards_in_flight 0
# HELP mqttd_replication_desired Configured replication factor R for durable placement groups.
# TYPE mqttd_replication_desired gauge
mqttd_replication_desired 3
# HELP mqttd_replication_min_actual Smallest replica-set size any placement group currently has — the worst-case durability; below replication_desired means at least one group is under-replicated (issue #167).
# TYPE mqttd_replication_min_actual gauge
mqttd_replication_min_actual 3
# HELP mqttd_replication_write_floor Smallest replica set a durable append may commit on (issue #239); replication_min_actual < replication_write_floor means durable writes are being REFUSED — QoS>=1 publishers get no ack and redeliver, retained mutations queue.
# TYPE mqttd_replication_write_floor gauge
mqttd_replication_write_floor 2
# HELP mqttd_retained_tombstones Retained tombstone fences currently held awaiting cluster-wide convergence (issue #229); sustained growth means an absent durable member or chronic divergence.
# TYPE mqttd_retained_tombstones gauge
mqttd_retained_tombstones 0
# HELP mqttd_misplaced_sessions Live persistent sessions hosted on a node that does NOT own their placement group (issue #284). Non-zero for longer than a convergence window means sessions that cannot be rehomed (the owner's peer address is unknown) — those sessions are undeliverable and their publishers are withheld.
# TYPE mqttd_misplaced_sessions gauge
mqttd_misplaced_sessions 0
# HELP mqttd_members Cluster members by SWIM state (alive/suspect/dead).
# TYPE mqttd_members gauge
mqttd_members{state="suspect"} 0
mqttd_members{state="alive"} 3
mqttd_members{state="dead"} 0
# HELP mqttd_lease_leader 1 if this node is the leader of its lease group, else 0.
